---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { BOOKING_URL } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Services | My Myo"
			description="Clinical Myotherapy, dry needling, manual lymphatic drainage, remedial massage and exercise rehabilitation with James Maddock in Carlton North, Melbourne."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Services</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Every appointment begins with assessment — history, orthopaedic and neurological
				testing where indicated — so treatment addresses what's driving your
				presentation, not just where it hurts.
			</p>

			<h2>Clinical Myotherapy</h2>
			<p>
				Myotherapy is the assessment, treatment, and management of musculoskeletal pain and
				dysfunction. A session can draw on:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Orthopaedic and neurological assessment, with standardised outcome measures</li>
				<li>Joint mobilisation and Muscle Energy Techniques</li>
				<li>Myofascial release and trigger point therapy</li>
				<li>Dry needling and electrical dry needling (within my Myotherapy scope)</li>
				<li>Myofascial cupping and instrument-assisted soft tissue work</li>
				<li>Neurodynamic mobilisation</li>
				<li>Exercise prescription and rehabilitation, delivered in a fully equipped clinic space</li>
				<li>Taping — kinesiology and rigid strapping</li>
				<li>Pain neuroscience education, so you understand what your pain means</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				New to myotherapy? Read
				<a href="/what-is-myotherapy">what Clinical Myotherapy actually is</a>,
				and how it differs from the professions next door.
			</p>

			<h2>Manual Lymphatic Drainage (MLD)</h2>
			<p>
				I've provided MLD continuously since 2007, across chronic illness, surgical
				recovery, gastrointestinal conditions, and oncological support including
				post-treatment lymphoedema management. Initial MLD appointments are 90 minutes,
				including 20–30 minutes of history-taking and education about your lymphatic
				system before any hands-on work.
			</p>
			<p>
				Note: I don't fit medical compression garments — if you need a garment
				prescription I'll refer you to an appropriately credentialled practitioner.
			</p>

			<h2>Remedial Massage</h2>
			<p>
				Nearly two decades of full-scope remedial massage remains the foundation of
				everything above. My long-standing remedial practice lives at
				<a href="https://massage.melbourne" target="_blank">massage.melbourne</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>Who I work with</h2>
			<p>
				I have particular experience with hypermobility and hEDS, perimenopause and
				menopause, neurodivergent clients, oncology-adjacent support, and trans and
				gender-diverse clients. Read about
				<a href="/who-i-work-with">who I work with, and how that experience shapes
				treatment</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>Referrals, not guesswork</h2>
			<p>
				If something falls outside my scope, I'll say so and refer you onward — GP,
				physiotherapy, exercise physiology, podiatry, or a credentialled lymphoedema
				therapist as appropriate. I keep a curated referral network so you land with
				the right person.
			</p>

			<p>
				<a class="cta-button" href={BOOKING_URL} target="_blank">Book an appointment</a>
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
